"summary": "The Parent Atlas summarization flow is a multi-stage pipeline that ingests packet feature envelopes, derives parent-atlas feature IDs, compresses them via a TurboVec compression plan, and generates summaries with Gemma4. Key components include scripts/atlas/parent-atlas-turbovec-compression-plan.mjs (TurboVec compression planning), scripts/atlas/gemma4-parent-atlas-summaries.mjs (Gemma4 summarization), sveltekit-frontend/src/lib/server/generation/packet-summary-pipeline.ts (packet summary pipeline), and scripts/atlas/graphify-summary-ranking-pipeline.mjs (summary ranking). The flow integrates with the graph traversal API (src/routes/api/graph/traverse/+server.ts), code intelligence datastore (src/lib/server/ace/codeintel-datastore.ts), and context-for-file (src/lib/server/atlas/context-for-file.ts). The P4 Gap Analysis provides a summary index using Self-Organizing Maps (SOM) and Autoencoders (AE) for dimensionality reduction and visualization. The overall pipeline follows a phased execution model (Phase A: status/commands, Phase B: execution-ready, Phase 2: multivector enrichment, Phase 3: execution pipeline map, Phase 4: gap analysis).",
